1. Conveyor with Permanent or other well aligned structures with normal maintenance
2. Temporary, portable, or poorly aligned conveyors. Also for cold weather conveyor less than zero continuously.</td></tr><tr><td width="5">13</td><td>Input Friction Factor</td><td>Input Fraction Factor is filled out</td></tr><tr><td width="5">14</td><td>Select Surcharge Angle from drop down list </td><td>Value is selected</td></tr><tr><td width="5">15</td><td>Select Drive Pully surface from Details drop down list </td><td>Value is selected</td></tr><tr><td width="5">16</td><td>Input Length Factor</td><td>Length factor is filled out</td></tr><tr><td width="5">17</td><td>At Idler Offset Type drop down list select a  value</td><td>Value is selected</td></tr><tr><td width="5">18</td><td>At Take Up Details drop down list select a value</td><td>Take Up Details is selected</td></tr><tr><td width="5">19</td><td>Select station field radio button </td><td>User should able to select radio button</td></tr><tr><td width="5">20</td><td>Click Save & Close</td><td>Conveyor name is displayed at the top of the conveyors list with the up arrow</td></tr><tr><td width="5">21</td><td>Click in the Up arrow,</td><td>Device is synchronized, conveyor saved into database and conveyor information visible from any mobile device or web browser.</td></tr><tr><td width="20%" valign="top"><span class="label">Execution type:</span></td><td colspan="3">Manual</td></tr>
